{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3459","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3459","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3459\",\"parent_revision\":\"aeb2feb72ddef6a53028cec5cbc7cb865eeb0f6abca8ec4b414a212c8a850625\",\"root_revision\":\"aeb2feb72ddef6a53028cec5cbc7cb865eeb0f6abca8ec4b414a212c8a850625\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## What\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`uv run pytest plugins/development-harness` fails eight tests. They are not caused by the work-ledger slice (#3449); each reproduces identically on a clean worktree at the commit before that work landed.\\n\\n```text\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_tiktoken_offline_safe.py::test_cl100k_base_is_cached_after_conftest\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py::TestOverBudgetGateHonoursNarrowing::test_over_budget_section_filter_returns_section_body\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py::TestOverBudgetGateHonoursNarrowing::test_over_budget_numeric_section_returns_section_body\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py::TestOverBudgetGateHonoursNarrowing::test_over_budget_sections_filter_returns_named_sections\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py::TestUnboundedOverBudgetStillReturnsDirectory::test_unbounded_large_but_compressible_body_delivered_inline\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_view_pagination_section_index.py::TestOverBudgetMeasurementExcludesDuplicatedContent::test_headed_under_budget_body_delivered_inline_despite_sections_dup\\nbacklog_core/tests/test_import_boundaries.py::test_operations_imports_before_server_without_cycle\\ntests/test_tool_output_schemas.py::test_output_schemas_stay_within_token_budget\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## How This Was Established\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNot assumed from the names. A detached worktree was created at the pre-ledger commit and the same eight node ids were run there:\\n\\n```bash\\ngit worktree add /tmp/baseline-dh <pre-ledger-sha>\\ncd /tmp/baseline-dh && uv run --project <repo> pytest <the five files> -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov -q\\n# 8 failed, 22 passed\\n```\\n\\nThe same five files on the ledger branch give the same eight failures, so the count and the identities match exactly.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Shape Of The Failures\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo clusters, likely two causes:\\n\\n1. **Token-budget measurement** \u2014 six failures across `test_tiktoken_offline_safe`, `test_view_over_budget_gate`, `test_view_pagination_section_index` and `test_tool_output_schemas`. All four files measure content against a token budget, and the first is specifically about whether the `cl100k_base` encoding is cached by conftest. A tokeniser that is not cached, or is falling back to a different estimate offline, would move every budget measurement at once. Worth checking that hypothesis before treating the six as separate bugs.\\n2. **Import ordering** \u2014 `test_operations_imports_before_server_without_cycle` asserts `backlog_core/operations.py` imports cleanly before `server.py` without a cycle.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Is Filed Rather Than Fixed Here\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThey sit in `backlog_core/`, which the work-ledger slice does not touch, and the repository's `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` is explicit that bugs in that package should be diagnosed against that document first rather than patched at the instance. That reading is the first step, not a fix attempt.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Suggested First Step\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun the six budget failures with the tokeniser cache warm and then cold, and confirm whether cluster 1 collapses to the single `cl100k_base` caching cause. If it does, this is one fix and one regression test, not six.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4f31de3deadf2ff1fec33cf1941a0e68e7b289d01975d2b4b2db02cf7fe13f2f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIydOQ\"}"}